# status: draft (2026-11-05), waiting for the owner's approval
# More people in Elderroot Village (owner request: more to explore): Bram the smith, Wenna the miller and Pell, a
# farm boy. No quests yet: a short talk each, and remarks in passing. Names are drafts (dialogue/glossary.md).
# Phase 8b (draft, 2026-11-07): a Rank Day line each while the prologue runs.
# Only GameState, QuestManager, Inventory, PlayerData, DragonManager, Cutscene and AudioManager may be called.

~ bram
if GameState.has_flag("prologue_active")
	Bram: Rank Day, eh? Go on, little spark. Show that old rock what you've got.
	=> END
if DragonManager.is_hatched()
	Bram: Ha! A dragon. Keep it away from my coal pile, Aurelia. It's already eyeing it.
	=> END
Bram: Morning, little spark. Mind the anvil, it bites.
- What are you making?
	Bram: Hinges. Nails. A pot for Maren. Nothing that'd make a story.
	Bram: [#worried] Though... I've had travellers asking for swords lately. Strange times.
- Could you teach me smithing?
	Bram: You? Ha. Your hands are made for spellbooks. Leave the hammering to me.
=> END

~ bram_bark
% Bram: Hot iron waits for no one!
% Bram: Mind the sparks.
=> END

~ wenna
if GameState.has_flag("prologue_active")
	Wenna: [#happy] Off to the Stone, dear? I'll bake something for after. Win or lose.
	=> END
if GameState.has_flag("warden_defeated")
	Wenna: [#happy] They're saying you sent a whole Emberbound captain running! My, my. Flour's on the house.
	=> END
Wenna: Aurelia, dear. Have you seen Dumpling? Grey cat. Round. Judgemental.
- He's on the mill roof again.
	Wenna: [#happy] Of course he is. Thank you, dear.
- I'll keep an eye out.
	Wenna: Bless you. He comes down for fish. Eventually.
Wenna: [#worried] And do be careful in the north woods. Odd folk with red banners have been camping there.
=> END

~ wenna_bark
% Wenna: Dumpling! Dumpling, come down!
% Wenna: Flour, flour, everywhere...
=> END

~ pell
if GameState.has_flag("prologue_active")
	Pell: My rank is Glimmer! Two marks! ...What do you think you'll get, Aurelia?
	=> END
Pell: Aurelia! Did you see the old watchtower, east past the pond? My grandad says it's haunted.
- Haunted by what?
	Pell: [#happy] Wisps! Little fire ones. They float around it at night. Brr!
- Towers don't get haunted.
	Pell: That's what a haunted tower WANTS you to think.
=> END

~ pell_bark
% Pell: The scarecrow moved. I swear it moved.
% Pell: Hollin Farm has the best honey. Don't tell Maren I said that.
=> END
